{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/616987-sell-me-on-scion","id":616987,"title":"Sell me on Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-05T18:01:56-07:00","id":616987,"title":"Sell me on Scion","content":"im huge into heroic stuff, when someone told me it was American Gods The Roleplaying Game i was very interesting. a friend got me the basic book and im thinking about running it or not. My main questions are, Do you need to be a Buff on Mythos to run it properly?<br /> do you Must have Demi God and God in order to run a more proper game?<br /> Whats eyecatching about the game acording to you (the players and Dms)<br /> any recomendations to someone who is into mythology but still having amateur-ish knowledges about it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T19:05:52-07:00","id":617025,"title":"","content":"Demigod and God are needed (or at least very valuable) for the higher power levels.<br /> How much do you to need know about mythology? Depends on which cultures you want to use most in your game. I knew almost nothing about the Aztec gods before I stated playing Scion. Don't know shit about Voodoo? Neither do most people. If you don't feel like doing research on the subject, just leave the Loa out of your story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T10:46:58-07:00","id":617874,"title":"","content":"Mangle's pretty much got it nailed.<br /> <br /> Knowledge of mythology is helpful, if you want games that really capture the feeling of the ancient myths. On the other hand, you can just as easily base the gods off pop-cultural versions of the gods if you wish. Hercules the Legendary Journeys? Sure. Why not? I'm not terribly familiar with American Gods, but as I do believe that's another perfectly fine example of what you can do with Scion.<br /> <br /> If you want to be as mythologically accurate as possible, there are books and web sites all over the place that can fill you in. But again, it's not absolutely essential. Take the gods in the books and do what you like with them.<br /> <br /> Demigod and God are absolutely necessary if you intend to have your players advance to the higher levels of power. It should be mentioned, however, that Scion's system really starts to fall apart at the higher levels. I have yet to meet a Scion group that doesn't have to do a LOT of houseruling to make the game work. There is a Second Edition in the works right now, so you might want to keep your eyes open for that when it's ready.<br /> <br /> What is eye-catching about the game to players? Power. LOTS of power. Scion is one of the most high-powered games in the RPG world. Also? If players like high-octane action in a setting where the old world of myth and the modern world collide, then Scion is definitely for them.<br /> <br /> For ST's? It can be a challenge dealing with players and NPC's that are as powerful as Scions can become. Plus, there's the appeal of telling modern myths and playing with the epic action and romance of the mythological world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T07:39:12-07:00","id":619985,"title":"","content":"Hero, Demi God and God are all part of a continuing story arc that follows your character's path towards divinity. So while you don't actually <b>need</b> Demi God and God to enjoy the game, you'll be stuck with low level characters if you run a strictly Hero game. There is also a 4th book called Ragnarok that revolves around the end of the world.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't know much about mythology, the books should have at least some introduction to the pantheons. In fact, one of the books includes the Atlantean pantheon who I believe are completely made up, rather than being from a real world religion.<br /> <br /> <br /> The game has a pretty large collection of pantheons to choose from. You may not have heard of all of them, but you should at least be familiar with one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Greek</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Egyptian</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Celtic</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Japanese</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Chinese</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Norse</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Yankee</b> (American) Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Allied</b> (British / France / Russian) Pantheon.<br /> <br /> <b>Aztec</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Voodoo</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Hindu</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <b>Persian</b> Pantheon<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Yankee Pantheon includes American folk tale heroes. Like Paul Bunyan, the guy who dug the Grand Canyon. Yeah, you can be his kid! Or better yet, you can be the child of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IhnUgAaea4M\" target=\"_blank\">Uncle Sam</a> himself!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And you don't have to base your game around real world religions either, the game has details on how to create your own player made pantheon as well. Not familiar with any of the official religions? <b>Make up your own!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What's eye catching to me about the game is that it is essentially White Wolf's version of a super hero game. Your characters will become massively powerful in this game, to the point where they can obliterate anything the World of Darkness can throw at them. I even read one example of a character who can lift a skyscraper over his head. Your characters are the children of gods, and the game involves their journey to become gods, while at the same time battling the Titans who threaten to destroy the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-08-2015, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T02:08:46-07:00","id":623196,"title":"","content":"Hope we helped pique your interest further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T06:42:11-07:00","id":624219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/616987-sell-me-on-scion?p=619985#post619985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yankee Pantheon includes American folk tale heroes. Like Paul Bunyan, the guy who dug the Grand Canyon. Yeah, you can be his kid! Or better yet, you can be the child of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IhnUgAaea4M\" target=\"_blank\">Uncle Sam</a> himself!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one thing that really bugs me about the game.<br /> <br /> 'We have a pantheon for a relatively young country sorted out, now to move onto the British, French, and Russian ones!'<br /> <br /> 'Cool, should we include King Arthur or Charlemagne?'<br /> <br /> 'Nah, nobody knows them, it'll be fine.'<br /> <br /> So I can play the child of these two people I've never heard of, but not my favourite mythological hero since I was a child who is known the world over, because the American pantheon (and not a native American one, which are cool and I'm happy I'll be introduced to one in 2e!) is somehow twice the size of pantheons with several times their history.<br /> <br /> So you know what would be more exicting than being a child of 'random dude who dug the Grand Canyon'? Being a child of King Arthur, or Gawain, or even Lancelot if you want to include the French! Because if Arthur hasn't awoken now, I'm terrified to think of what the future in the Scionverse has planned for Britain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you don't have to base your game around real world religions either, the game has details on how to create your own player made pantheon as well. Not familiar with any of the official religions? <b>Make up your own!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Although the coolest part? Playing around with real world mythology. Is your guy badass enough to be the Scion of Thor, or the Dagda, or Baal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's eye catching to me about the game is that it is essentially White Wolf's version of a super hero game. Your characters will become massively powerful in this game, to the point where they can obliterate anything the World of Darkness can throw at them. I even read one example of a character who can lift a skyscraper over his head. Your characters are the children of gods, and the game involves their journey to become gods, while at the same time battling the Titans who threaten to destroy the world. </div> </div> </div>Eh, WW did a superhero game, called Abberrant. Scion is the original superheroes once again walking the earth and beating up monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:02:42-07:00","id":624238,"title":"","content":"Well you can be the scion of Robin Hood, so that's pretty cool. Though rather than Arthur, I'd want the chance to be a scion of Merlin and just wreck the Titans with the flick of my wrist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Oh no, the Titan is attacking that city. *boop* oh hey, now its a fish!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The only members of the Allied Pantheon I've even heard off are John Bull, Robin Hood, and Baba Yaga.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:21:01-07:00","id":624261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/616987-sell-me-on-scion?p=624238#post624238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only members of the Allied Pantheon I've even heard off are John Bull, Robin Hood, and Baba Yaga.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. IIRC some of them feel more like anthropomorphic personifications more than a deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T08:24:16-07:00","id":624382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/616987-sell-me-on-scion?p=624238#post624238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you can be the scion of Robin Hood, so that's pretty cool. Though rather than Arthur, I'd want the chance to be a scion of Merlin and just wreck the Titans with the flick of my wrist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be honest, I'm surprised the Arthurian Mythos wasn't featured in any fashion, you could probably do an entire pantheon with it (add in the matter of France if you just want a knightly pantheon). Considering they included a nine Pantheon deity of which I've never even heard of seven of them, and the other two I only know of because I've heard the name used in that context in passing, they really could have beefed up the deities in the 'allied pantheon' (more on why this one makes me mad later).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Oh no, the Titan is attacking that city. *boop* oh hey, now its a fish!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Not really Merlin's magic, but you'll probably get a lot of fun out of the animal and illusion purviews, to eventually being able to pull this off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only members of the Allied Pantheon I've even heard off are John Bull, Robin Hood, and Baba Yaga. </div> </div> </div>Let's see, I've heard of:<br /> <br /> Britannia, Robin Hood, D'Artagnan*, and Baba Yaga, I might have heard of John Bull in passing but he's not really known in my area of England.<br /> <br /> But seriously, you take mythological figures from 3 countries, and decide that in order to be American and promote America, as well as the idea that America won the Second World War (which is not true, they helped, but likely couldn't have done it on their own), you'll take the 1000+ years of history each has, and pick 3 figures, leaving out the most well known ones? In Britain there are many historical and fictional figures you could add to their pantheon, and I'm sure the same can be said for France (Scarlet Pimpernel springs to mind, as does that Charlemagne fellow) and Russia. I don't have enough time to research British Myth to pull together more than a 4/5 member pantheon off the top of my head, but it really shouldn't be hard. You can probably get Beowulf in there as well, how cool would that be?<br /> <br /> * never heard of The Three Musketeers? He's the fourth one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T15:05:19-07:00","id":624655,"title":"","content":"Well likewise I've only heard of John Bull in passing, and the only thing I know about Baba is she's an old witch who lives in a walking house and people should stay the hell away from her.<br /> <br /> As for the Yankee pantheon, it's been a long time since I read any American folk lore, but here's what I remember about them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Paul Bunyan</b> - A giant lumberjack who dug the grand canyon by himself. He did many other feats too, but the grand canyon is the only one I can remember off the top of my head. His travel companion was Babe, the big, blue Ox.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Johnny Appleseed</b> - Story goes he's responsible for all the apple trees in America, as he took it upon himself to travel the country planting their seeds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pecos Bill</b> - I think this guy wrestled a tornado into submission by lassoing it and riding it like a bronco.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>John Henry</b> - A railroad worker who wanted to prove the human spirit was stronger than technological marvels. He worked himself to death trying to build a railroad through a mountain before a machine could do the job.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Br'er Rabbit</b> - I think this guy is attributed to a very racist story known as The Tar Baby.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Uncle Sam</b> - I thought this guy was just an American Icon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Betsy Ross</b> - I think she designed our flag.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Columbia</b> - Unless they rule 63'd Christopher Columbus, I don't know who she is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rosie the Riveter</b> - Never heard the name before!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T22:37:06-07:00","id":625132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/616987-sell-me-on-scion?p=624655#post624655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Paul Bunyan</b> - A giant lumberjack who dug the grand canyon by himself. He did many other feats too, but the grand canyon is the only one I can remember off the top of my head. His travel companion was Babe, the big, blue Ox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Canyon was an accident, he was dragging his axe along behind him.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Johnny Appleseed</b> - Story goes he's responsible for all the apple trees in America, as he took it upon himself to travel the country planting their seeds. </div> </div> </div>Based on a real guy, named John Chapman.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Pecos Bill</b> - I think this guy wrestled a tornado into submission by lassoing it and riding it like a bronco. </div> </div> </div>The Sky boon Tornado Tamer is based on that story.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>John Henry</b> - A railroad worker who wanted to prove the human spirit was stronger than technological marvels. He worked himself to death trying to build a railroad through a mountain before a machine could do the job. </div> </div> </div>True story. And he WON. A personal favorite, his story exemplifies America's can-do spirit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Br'er Rabbit</b> - I think this guy is attributed to a very racist story known as The Tar Baby. </div> </div> </div>Part of a larger story that was coded messages for escaping slavery.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Uncle Sam</b> - I thought this guy was just an American Icon. </div> </div> </div>True, but I still think he's cool. In my head canon, he is an ascended Scion of King Arthur.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Betsy Ross</b> - I think she designed our flag. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't know why the thought she should be a part of the Pantheon.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Columbia</b> - Unless they rule 63'd Christopher Columbus, I don't know who she is. </div> </div> </div>A.K.A. Lady Liberty. You know that big copper statue in New York? Also, a Scion of Athena per the book.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Rosie the Riveter</b> - Never heard the name before! </div> </div> </div>Icon, like Uncle Sam. Represented women's contributions to the war effort, somewhat of a feminist icon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one